- op: discuss  # 36ea
  at: '2026-10-03T06:42:04Z'  # 36ea
  by: agent  # 36ea
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 36ea
  clock: 3  # 36ea
  nonce: 36ea  # 36ea
  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE: the title's \"emits no call edge\" stopped being true on 2026-09-26. Title updated.\n- dbec60fb68 (INV-bamij, \"emit external calls, and anchor a field lambda's calls on its class\") sends any call NOT inside a method to the enclosing type, else the file (csharp.py:1450-1454). _get_enclosing_method (csharp.py:1183) recognises only method_declaration and constructor_declaration, so an accessor's calls are emitted but credited to the CLASS.\n- Repro: properties Getter {get{return Helper();}}, Setter {set{_v=Helper();}}, Twice => Helper()*2, AutoInit {get;} = Helper2(). Result: A(class) -> A.Helper 0.85 and A(class) -> A.Helper2 0.85 (the three accessor calls collapse into one class edge), control A.Run -> A.Helper, and zero edges from any kind=property symbol.\n- WIDER FAMILY: indexers (this[int]), operators, destructors and event add/remove accessors produce NO symbol, and their calls also go to the class. Separately, a local-function call (Loc() inside M) resolves to external_symbol Loc.\n- The call-anchor gate fixture (test_call_anchor_gate.py:45) registers C# only through test_csharp_one_leaf_name_in_two_classes; no property case.\n- The 201/0 figures predate dbec60fb68 and need re-measuring. The ask stands: anchor the call on the property, by position."  # 36ea
- op: discuss  # 5650
  at: '2026-10-04T10:36:27Z'  # 5650
  by: agent  # 5650
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5650
  clock: 4  # 5650
  nonce: '5650'  # 5650
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-04 (stage 8b agent). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/binap (worktree ~/hg_wt/binap, based on stage-8 integration 2a98abb55d, NOT pushed), commit 5940353412. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/binap.md.\n\nPremise re-verified at 2a98abb55d (live repro, analyze_csharp): every accessor call (get / set / => / initialiser) went to the CLASS; indexer, operator, conversion operator, destructor and event-with-accessors had no symbol; new B() in a getter emitted NO instantiates edge.\n\nFix: one set _CSHARP_MEMBER_BODY_NODES (method, constructor, property, indexer, operator, conversion operator, destructor, event) read by core enclosing_declared_symbol, by POSITION (INV-midag); _get_enclosing_method deleted. New symbols: indexer kind=subscript (Type.this[]), operator / conversion operator / destructor kind=method (Type.operator+, Type.operator int, Type.~Type), event-with-accessors kind=event. A property owns its initialiser; a FIELD initialiser stays on the class (INV-bamij). Call-anchor gate gains test_csharp_member_bodies_are_anchored_on_their_member.\n\nTests: red 12 failed / 17 passed on the base sources, then green; affected run (616 files) 21,389 passed + 1 failed (spec symbol_meta count, fixed in the pony commit), scoped coverage 100%; final targeted run 333 passed.\n\nA/B by call site on the 8 C# corpus repos: 73 call sites moved class -> containing member (54 property, 18 destructor, 1 operator==), +1 instantiates from a getter, 0 lost, containment violations 0 both arms; property-sourced edges 0 -> 55. No event-with-accessors or conversion operator occurs in the corpus (fixture-only).\n\nResiduals filed: WI-sisuv (field-initialiser object creation dropped, local-function call external, field-like event no symbol), WI-kajoh (records emit no symbol), WI-rokir (kotlin accessors, same family). Swift deinit/observers noted on WI-sogof."  # 5650
